Capture this explicitly in lambdas that use it

These lambdas reach this through an implicit [=] capture, which C++20
deprecates. DART sets no language standard, so it builds as C++20 under
GCC 16, where that is the default, and DART's -Werror turns the warning
into an error. [this] (plus the one by-value bool) means the same thing and
is valid in both C++17 and C++20.

